scenario_id: dpgd-116
theme: house-md
run_id: 4
total_caught: 6
total_findings: 7
weighted_caught: 28
total_weight: 37
score_pct: 75.7
findings:
- finding_id: C1
  title: from_file_or_default swallows ALL errors including parse and permission failures
  weight: 8
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: 'No phase identified that from_file_or_default swallows all errors. The
    config_loading tests don''t distinguish NotFound from parse/permission errors,
    and the reviewer''s finding #9 about silent unknown fields is related but doesn''t
    cover the from_file_or_default error swallowing.'
- finding_id: I1
  title: CliError Display leaks internal details to stderr (CWE-209)
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: "Reviewer finding #7 flags CWE-209: 'cli_error_display_does_not_leak_server_internals\
    \ only asserts !display.is_empty(). That assertion is vacuous \u2014 it proves\
    \ nothing about information leakage.' However, the reviewer notes the Display\
    \ impl itself hides inner strings ('server error' not the inner String), so the\
    \ dev partially mitigated it but the test is vacuous."
- finding_id: I2
  title: "SiemClient.tenant_id uses raw String \u2014 header injection risk (CWE-113)"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: "Reviewer finding #2 (CRITICAL): 'validate_header_value() exists but is\
    \ never called in get() \u2014 CWE-113 defense is theater. A tenant ID of evil\\\
    r\\nX-Injected: yes would be injected directly into the HTTP request.' TEA wrote\
    \ header injection tests but they only test the validator function in isolation,\
    \ not that it's wired into the client. The reviewer caught the wiring gap."
- finding_id: I3
  title: Dependencies use direct version strings instead of workspace = true
  weight: 3
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: "Reviewer finding #4: 'toml = \"0.8\" not workspace-managed, spec requires\
    \ 0.9' \u2014 identifies at least one dep not using workspace = true. However,\
    \ the reviewer only flagged toml specifically, not all 6 deps mentioned in the\
    \ ground truth."
- finding_id: I4
  title: "Config token field silently ignored \u2014 secret left on disk"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: "Reviewer finding #9: 'RawConfig silently ignores unknown fields \u2014\
    \ no #[serde(deny_unknown_fields)]. A config file with passwrd = \"secret\" (typo)\
    \ will silently use defaults instead of warning the operator.'"
- finding_id: I5
  title: "Vacuously true test \u2014 assertion is None || true"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: 'Reviewer finding #10: ''exit_code_success_is_zero asserts 0 == 0. This
    literally asserts zero equals zero. It doesn''t test any code.'' While the ground
    truth refers to a different vacuously true test (None || true pattern), the reviewer
    also caught finding #7 about the vacuous CWE-209 assertion. However, the specific
    I5 finding about assert!(config.server().is_none() || ...) was not explicitly
    called out.'
- finding_id: I6
  title: "Test with zero assertions \u2014 only checks non-panic"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: "Reviewer finding #11: 'header_value_handles_tabs test has no assertion\
    \ \u2014 let _ = result. The comment says either accept or reject, but must not\
    \ panic \u2014 but there's no assertion. This is not a test; it's a comment with\
    \ extra steps.'"
